I'm assuming two things.  First, although you didn't specify any
system in your post, it sounds as though you're playing on a Unix
machine.  Second, it sounds as though the game process is still
running.  If not, ignore the rest of this post.

The thing to do is to check and see if you still have control of the
process.  If so, terminate it, nicely if possible.  If not, ask
someone with superuser access to do so.  Unless something happens to
the filesystem, nethack always saves on termination, so there should
be no problem with keeping your character.

